1
00:00:05,082 --> 00:00:06,603
You wake up

2
00:00:08,606 --> 00:00:10,128
Leave me alone

3
00:00:10,409 --> 00:00:12,371
Yeah，like that'
s gonna happen

4
00:00:12,411 --> 00:00:13,773
Now get up

5
00:00:13,813 --> 00:00:15,776
We can still do
this the easy way

6
00:00:15,816 --> 00:00:17,858
Come on
this isn't a hotel

7
00:00:20,142 --> 00:00:21,703
Don't touch me

8
00:00:23,386 --> 00:00:24,907
How dare you？

9
00:00:25,389 --> 00:00:27,871
Do you have any
idea who I am？

10
00:01:54,817 --> 00:01:56,017
Alright

11
00:01:56,258 --> 00:01:58,298
here's all the
stuff you came in with

12
00:01:58,819 --> 00:01:59,819
If everything
's in order

13
00:01:59,859 --> 00:02:01,259
you can sign here

14
00:02:05,060 --> 00:02:06,261
Miss Heine Mon

15
00:02:06,301 --> 00:02:09,182
I don't ever want
to see you tossed in the cooler again

16
00:02:09,222 --> 00:02:11,983
Passing out drunk
alone in a dark alley

17
00:02:12,023 --> 00:02:14,943
Be thankful something horrible didn't happen to you

18
00:02:15,064 --> 00:02:16,664
You got a
cigarette？

19
00:02:16,704 --> 00:02:18,104
Huh？

20
00:02:18,144 --> 00:02:20,945
I'm just asking
if you've got a cigarette

21
00:02:25,485 --> 00:02:27,525
There's no
smoking in the station

22
00:02:27,565 --> 00:02:29,125
Go outside if
you want to smoke

23
00:02:56,851 --> 00:02:57,972
Lighter

24
00:02:58,576 --> 00:03:00,380
Where's
my lighter？

25
00:03:02,891 --> 00:03:04,011
My bag

26
00:03:05,132 --> 00:03:07,572
I wanna know what
you did with my bag

27
00:03:07,972 --> 00:03:10,413
And I already
told you it's the only bag you had

28
00:03:10,453 --> 00:03:11,173
You liar

29
00:03:11,213 --> 00:03:12,614
I know you're not
telling me the truth

30
00:03:12,654 --> 00:03:13,894
I had another
shoulder bag

31
00:03:13,934 --> 00:03:14,814
where is it？

32
00:03:14,854 --> 00:03:16,495
Probably with
whoever stole it from you

33
00:03:16,535 --> 00:03:18,735
When you passed
out drunk in the alley

34
00:03:18,775 --> 00:03:20,055
What are you
going to do about it？

35
00:03:20,095 --> 00:03:20,856
I had valuables

36
00:03:20,896 --> 00:03:22,496
important
things in there

37
00:03:22,536 --> 00:03:23,976
I'll tell you what

38
00:03:24,016 --> 00:03:26,697
You can fill out
a theft report if you like

39
00:03:27,097 --> 00:03:29,578
But I really
wouldn't get your hopes up

40
00:03:35,599 --> 00:03:38,242
How the hell did
you lose your keys？

41
00:03:38,684 --> 00:03:40,286
My bag was
stolen last night

42
00:03:40,326 --> 00:03:42,528
Just hurry up and
open the room for me

43
00:03:47,817 --> 00:03:48,378
What…

44
00:03:48,418 --> 00:03:50,139
what
happened here？

45
00:03:52,367 --> 00:03:53,247
Damn

46
00:03:53,287 --> 00:03:55,807
somebody
really went to town

47
00:03:56,448 --> 00:03:57,128
Oh，man

48
00:03:57,168 --> 00:03:58,408
this is awful

49
00:03:58,448 --> 00:04:00,369
I gotta
change the lock now

50
00:04:00,409 --> 00:04:01,209
Which reminds me

51
00:04:01,249 --> 00:04:01,889
Miss Heinemann

52
00:04:01,929 --> 00:04:03,770
you still owe
me back rent

53
00:04:03,810 --> 00:04:05,610
I don't want to
have to ask you again

54
00:04:05,650 --> 00:04:08,091
The deposit you
put down has already run out

55
00:04:08,131 --> 00:04:10,732
I'm gonna need
the rest of what you owe soon

56
00:04:11,412 --> 00:04:14,213
These people even
broke into my damn suitcase

57
00:04:14,253 --> 00:04:15,853
Are you listening？

58
00:04:15,893 --> 00:04:19,094
You have to pay
for a new lock and all that back rent

59
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:21,781
Well，I don't
have any money

60
00:04:21,821 --> 00:04:22,821
What？

61
00:04:24,381 --> 00:04:25,302
Fine，I'll get out

62
00:04:25,342 --> 00:04:26,582
don't worry

63
00:04:28,182 --> 00:04:30,343
Such a
tragic story

64
00:04:30,943 --> 00:04:31,583
But still

65
00:04:31,623 --> 00:04:34,384
I don't know what
you expect me to do about any of it

66
00:04:34,424 --> 00:04:34,704
You know

67
00:04:34,744 --> 00:04:38,304
I seem to remember you being the one who stormed out on me

68
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:39,506
Oh，come on

69
00:04:39,546 --> 00:04:41,147
that's all
ancient history now

70
00:04:41,187 --> 00:04:42,989
So，why not
buy me a drink？

71
00:04:43,029 --> 00:04:44,070
Please， Ava

72
00:04:44,110 --> 00:04:45,351
That's just a
stolen purse

73
00:04:45,391 --> 00:04:46,632
for God's sake

74
00:04:46,672 --> 00:04:49,955
You must have had
some extra cash tucked away somewhere

75
00:04:50,036 --> 00:04:50,917
Honestly

76
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:52,198
I've yet to
meet another woman

77
00:04:52,238 --> 00:04:54,439
who could burn
through money the way you do

78
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:57,643
And here you are
finally coming to me for some cash

79
00:04:57,683 --> 00:04:58,604
This is it

80
00:04:58,644 --> 00:04:59,725
welcome to
rock bottom

81
00:04:59,765 --> 00:05:00,286
baby

82
00:05:00,326 --> 00:05:00,926
So，how much？

83
00:05:00,966 --> 00:05:03,008
Huh？

84
00:05:03,209 --> 00:05:04,049
I'll
sleep with you

85
00:05:04,089 --> 00:05:05,050
you know

86
00:05:06,119 --> 00:05:08,679
I'm asking you
how much you'd be willing to pay

87
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:11,400
My God

88
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:12,680
Honey
as a general rule

89
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:14,321
most men won't
pay to have sex

90
00:05:14,361 --> 00:05:16,841
with women they'
ve already had a bunch of times

91
00:05:19,322 --> 00:05:21,203
You can at
least buy me a drink

92
00:05:21,243 --> 00:05:24,003
Go find yourself
a street corner to work

93
00:05:24,083 --> 00:05:24,603
Who knows

94
00:05:24,643 --> 00:05:26,324
you might get
lucky and meet some sad sack

95
00:05:26,364 --> 00:05:27,844
who's not
too picky

96
00:05:28,084 --> 00:05:28,645
Desperate

97
00:05:28,685 --> 00:05:31,565
middleaged and
drunk must be someone's type

98
00:06:10,758 --> 00:06:11,079
Yeah

99
00:06:11,119 --> 00:06:14,441
I'm positive you
didn't leave any purse here last night

100
00:06:14,481 --> 00:06:16,523
Maybe you left it
wherever you went next

101
00:06:16,563 --> 00:06:19,245
I don't remember
anything after I left this bar

102
00:06:19,285 --> 00:06:22,327
You mentioned you
had something important in your bag

103
00:06:22,367 --> 00:06:23,448
If it's
worth any money

104
00:06:23,488 --> 00:06:25,649
you might as
well kiss it goodbye

105
00:06:27,085 --> 00:06:27,926
No，it's not

106
00:06:27,966 --> 00:06:30,048
it's not worth
anything at all

107
00:06:30,529 --> 00:06:31,330
Not any money

108
00:06:31,370 --> 00:06:32,451
that is

109
00:06:41,182 --> 00:06:42,063
Hey

110
00:06:42,103 --> 00:06:43,664
I've been
looking for you

111
00:06:44,426 --> 00:06:46,429
I asked for you
at the pub back there

112
00:06:46,469 --> 00:06:49,592
And they told me
you just headed in this direction

113
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:51,434
Yeah，and
who are you？

114
00:06:52,345 --> 00:06:53,706
Are you serious？

115
00:06:53,827 --> 00:06:56,469
We had such a
good time drinking last night

116
00:06:57,111 --> 00:06:59,313
I was drinking with you？

117
00:06:59,834 --> 00:07:00,995
Your bag

118
00:07:01,356 --> 00:07:03,598
That's why I was
looking for you

119
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:06,242
I guess this
means I have to make

120
00:07:06,282 --> 00:07:08,164
awkward
introductions again？

121
00:07:09,606 --> 00:07:11,007
I'm Roberto

122
00:07:11,048 --> 00:07:11,729
So

123
00:07:11,769 --> 00:07:13,971
shall we grab a
little something to eat？

124
00:07:14,412 --> 00:07:16,053
Your hotel room？

125
00:07:16,093 --> 00:07:16,974
Really？

126
00:07:17,014 --> 00:07:17,894
That's terrible

127
00:07:17,934 --> 00:07:18,935
I'm so sorry

128
00:07:18,975 --> 00:07:19,775
Well，whatever

129
00:07:19,815 --> 00:07:21,856
I mean，it's not
like you did it

130
00:07:22,056 --> 00:07:22,617
Well，no

131
00:07:22,657 --> 00:07:23,617
obviously not

132
00:07:23,657 --> 00:07:25,858
I didn't even
dare look in your bag

133
00:07:25,978 --> 00:07:26,499
Oh，look

134
00:07:26,539 --> 00:07:28,500
my hotel keys
are still in here

135
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,220
A little
late for those

136
00:07:30,301 --> 00:07:31,781
I don't need
them anymore

137
00:07:31,821 --> 00:07:32,342
I'm sorry

138
00:07:32,382 --> 00:07:33,702
it's all my fault

139
00:07:33,742 --> 00:07:34,983
If I'd returned
your bag sooner

140
00:07:35,023 --> 00:07:37,584
You wouldn't have
been kicked out of your room in the first place

141
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:39,705
Hey，it wasn't
your fault at all

142
00:07:41,146 --> 00:07:41,666
Besides

143
00:07:41,706 --> 00:07:44,388
I'm very grateful
that you gave me back my bag

144
00:07:44,428 --> 00:07:45,068
Honestly

145
00:07:45,108 --> 00:07:47,549
I'm kind of
grateful that you lost it

146
00:07:48,310 --> 00:07:48,750
Well

147
00:07:48,790 --> 00:07:51,111
last night as I
watched you leave the pub

148
00:07:51,151 --> 00:07:52,792
I sat there
thinking to myself

149
00:07:52,832 --> 00:07:55,313
You shouldn't let
this person slip away

150
00:07:55,393 --> 00:07:57,154
And now
thanks to your bag

151
00:07:57,194 --> 00:07:59,275
here you are
and here I am

152
00:08:00,355 --> 00:08:02,316
You have something very important in there

153
00:08:02,356 --> 00:08:03,117
don't you？

154
00:08:03,157 --> 00:08:04,037
I do

155
00:08:08,333 --> 00:08:10,696
This is all that
I have left in the world

156
00:08:12,421 --> 00:08:13,102
係相簿？

157
00:08:13,142 --> 00:08:14,906
May I take a look？

158
00:08:14,946 --> 00:08:15,986
You may

159
00:08:21,277 --> 00:08:22,799
That's my father

160
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:26,001
He looks just
like I imagined

161
00:08:26,041 --> 00:08:28,162
He was a
hospital director，right？

162
00:08:28,202 --> 00:08:28,562
Yeah

163
00:08:28,602 --> 00:08:30,563
did I talk about
him last night？

164
00:08:30,603 --> 00:08:31,323
You did

165
00:08:31,363 --> 00:08:33,485
you spoke very
highly of him

166
00:08:33,525 --> 00:08:35,806
You mentioned
that he died ten years ago

167
00:08:35,846 --> 00:08:38,006
I could tell that
you still miss him

168
00:08:40,088 --> 00:08:41,728
Let's see，ah

169
00:08:41,769 --> 00:08:43,329
the exfiance？

170
00:08:44,370 --> 00:08:44,970
Please

171
00:08:45,010 --> 00:08:47,171
don't tell me I
told you about him

172
00:08:47,572 --> 00:08:49,973
I believe his
name was Tenma？

173
00:08:51,466 --> 00:08:52,627
Quite a guy

174
00:08:52,667 --> 00:08:54,028
this Tenma

175
00:08:54,068 --> 00:08:56,550
I really wanna
know what I said last night

176
00:08:56,590 --> 00:08:58,672
Well，I wouldn't
make a habit of it

177
00:08:58,712 --> 00:09:01,274
It might end up
making other men jealous

178
00:09:03,476 --> 00:09:04,436
Huh？

179
00:09:04,757 --> 00:09:06,839
Odd，this
page is empty

180
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:09,241
Is that so？

181
00:09:09,521 --> 00:09:11,563
The photos that
were on this page

182
00:09:11,603 --> 00:09:13,524
looks like
somebody tore them out

183
00:09:13,845 --> 00:09:14,045
Well

184
00:09:14,085 --> 00:09:16,767
I guess I didn't
need those pictures anymore

185
00:09:16,848 --> 00:09:18,048
So I see

186
00:09:18,776 --> 00:09:19,616
Hey

187
00:09:21,698 --> 00:09:23,298
Let's get a drink

188
00:09:24,179 --> 00:09:25,460
Sounds good

189
00:09:31,584 --> 00:09:31,985
So

190
00:09:32,025 --> 00:09:34,146
you were running
a security company？

191
00:09:34,186 --> 00:09:35,387
I'm impressed

192
00:09:35,427 --> 00:09:36,307
Yeah

193
00:09:36,347 --> 00:09:37,988
in the
south of France

194
00:09:40,758 --> 00:09:41,959
And then we
had a bad day

195
00:09:41,999 --> 00:09:44,963
and one of our
better clients was killed on my watch

196
00:09:45,003 --> 00:09:47,045
So，that was
the end of that

197
00:09:48,487 --> 00:09:50,610
We're both going
through tough times

198
00:09:50,650 --> 00:09:51,651
Nah，forget it

199
00:09:51,691 --> 00:09:53,334
let's drink to
the here and now

200
00:09:53,374 --> 00:09:54,335
Enjoy ourselves

201
00:09:54,375 --> 00:09:55,335
you know？

202
00:09:55,576 --> 00:09:56,617
Mhm

203
00:10:02,537 --> 00:10:03,417
Uh

204
00:10:03,897 --> 00:10:05,138
That song？

205
00:10:05,258 --> 00:10:06,019
It's good stuff

206
00:10:06,059 --> 00:10:06,979
huh？

207
00:10:07,219 --> 00:10:09,060
So you like
this song too？

208
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:10,301
Of course

209
00:10:10,981 --> 00:10:12,342
Let's dance

210
00:10:22,507 --> 00:10:23,508
Come on

211
00:10:23,548 --> 00:10:24,108
Well

212
00:10:24,148 --> 00:10:26,269
I don't really
know how to dance

213
00:10:27,470 --> 00:10:29,351
Just put your
arms around me

214
00:10:29,391 --> 00:10:30,151
Um…

215
00:10:34,335 --> 00:10:35,255
Good

216
00:10:36,336 --> 00:10:38,456
I knew a man who
loved this song

217
00:10:38,496 --> 00:10:40,937
He wasn't a very
good dancer either

218
00:10:41,817 --> 00:10:42,577
So

219
00:10:42,737 --> 00:10:44,857
you'd end up
dancing like this？

220
00:10:45,818 --> 00:10:46,978
That's right

221
00:10:53,582 --> 00:10:54,782
How fun

222
00:10:55,142 --> 00:10:56,662
How about
another drink？

223
00:10:56,702 --> 00:10:58,142
Just one more？

224
00:10:58,182 --> 00:10:58,863
Thanks

225
00:10:58,903 --> 00:11:00,423
but I'm good

226
00:11:00,863 --> 00:11:02,223
Lightweight

227
00:11:05,023 --> 00:11:06,463
Time for bed

228
00:11:06,743 --> 00:11:07,983
Sounds good to me

229
00:11:08,023 --> 00:11:08,943
babe

230
00:11:35,602 --> 00:11:38,085
Those photographs
you took out of the album

231
00:11:38,125 --> 00:11:39,565
Where'd you
hide them？

232
00:11:40,287 --> 00:11:43,690
Tell me，You see

233
00:11:43,730 --> 00:11:45,931
I'm onto your
little secret

234
00:11:46,893 --> 00:11:48,574
You're
looking for Tenma

235
00:11:48,734 --> 00:11:49,735
aren't you？

236
00:11:50,576 --> 00:11:52,658
I know you kept
those photos from burning

237
00:11:52,698 --> 00:11:55,220
And I'm sure you
have them with you somewhere

238
00:11:55,260 --> 00:11:55,821
What？

239
00:11:55,861 --> 00:11:56,862
You're saying

240
00:11:56,902 --> 00:11:58,743
you know
where Tenma is？

241
00:11:59,638 --> 00:12:07,637
Yeah

242
00:12:07,677 --> 00:12:10,397
The photographs
that you're talking about

243
00:12:10,677 --> 00:12:12,677
They're the ones
with father and that boy

244
00:12:12,717 --> 00:12:13,917
am I right？

245
00:12:14,597 --> 00:12:16,596
Johan，wasn't it？

246
00:12:19,436 --> 00:12:20,236
I've seen him

247
00:12:20,276 --> 00:12:21,196
you know

248
00:12:21,236 --> 00:12:22,676
Blonde，charming

249
00:12:22,716 --> 00:12:23,756
handsome

250
00:12:23,796 --> 00:12:25,315
He's grown up well

251
00:12:27,306 --> 00:12:29,627
我見過佢，一年前在杜塞爾多夫

252
00:12:33,872 --> 00:12:34,912
Kenzo

253
00:12:35,713 --> 00:12:37,274
Let's start over

254
00:12:37,875 --> 00:12:38,675
You…

255
00:12:39,516 --> 00:12:40,877
You need me

256
00:12:45,682 --> 00:12:46,722
Kenzo

257
00:12:50,406 --> 00:12:52,007
You belong to me

258
00:12:54,421 --> 00:12:56,303
I will
get you back

259
00:12:58,548 --> 00:13:00,430
Because
you're mine

260
00:13:07,441 --> 00:13:08,241
So

261
00:13:08,563 --> 00:13:10,285
what are you up
to these days？

262
00:13:10,406 --> 00:13:12,328
I've heard all
sorts of rumours

263
00:13:13,866 --> 00:13:15,990
The rumours
are probably true

264
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:18,754
I've been married
and divorced three times now

265
00:13:18,796 --> 00:13:21,321
Between my father'
s inheritance and my alimony

266
00:13:21,361 --> 00:13:23,205
I'm living
pretty comfortably

267
00:13:23,245 --> 00:13:24,287
But enough about me

268
00:13:24,327 --> 00:13:25,489
how has life
been treating you

269
00:13:25,529 --> 00:13:26,731
Dr， Becker？

270
00:13:27,453 --> 00:13:28,573
I dunno

271
00:13:28,693 --> 00:13:30,093
nothing's
changed with me

272
00:13:30,133 --> 00:13:32,572
I still have no
chance of moving up in the world

273
00:13:32,612 --> 00:13:33,412
Speaking of which

274
00:13:33,452 --> 00:13:35,452
Tenma's now
chief of surgery

275
00:13:35,492 --> 00:13:38,292
Word is he's on
his way to becoming hospital director

276
00:13:38,332 --> 00:13:39,292
Love to be
in his shoes

277
00:13:39,332 --> 00:13:40,531
let me tell you

278
00:13:40,571 --> 00:13:41,171
But please

279
00:13:41,211 --> 00:13:42,131
who am I kidding？

280
00:13:42,171 --> 00:13:43,371
It ain't so bad

281
00:13:43,411 --> 00:13:45,491
I still manage to
have a good time

282
00:13:45,531 --> 00:13:47,451
There's more to
life than promotions

283
00:13:47,491 --> 00:13:48,771
I'd never want
to be like Tenma

284
00:13:48,811 --> 00:13:50,570
and have no time
for women or fun

285
00:13:50,610 --> 00:13:51,930
What's the point？

286
00:13:54,177 --> 00:13:55,340
Is Kenzo…

287
00:13:55,907 --> 00:13:59,406
Do you know by any chance if Doctor Tenma ever did settle down？

288
00:13:59,446 --> 00:14:00,366
No，not yet

289
00:14:00,406 --> 00:14:01,566
and to be
completely honest

290
00:14:01,606 --> 00:14:04,286
I've introduced
him to quite a few very nice women

291
00:14:04,326 --> 00:14:05,126
But you know him

292
00:14:05,166 --> 00:14:06,166
no interest at all

293
00:14:06,206 --> 00:14:07,927
his work
comes first

294
00:14:08,167 --> 00:14:09,367
As a
matter of fact

295
00:14:09,407 --> 00:14:11,327
I'm about to set
him up with a new girl

296
00:14:11,367 --> 00:14:13,527
God only knows if
it's gonna work out

297
00:14:13,567 --> 00:14:15,247
She's the
daughter of a state senator

298
00:14:15,287 --> 00:14:18,047
and she is
absolutely beautiful

299
00:14:18,087 --> 00:14:19,527
If she can't
keep his attention

300
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:20,887
then I give up

301
00:14:20,927 --> 00:14:22,448
But，anyway

302
00:14:22,488 --> 00:14:23,968
you called me
about something

303
00:14:24,008 --> 00:14:25,208
How can I
be of service

304
00:14:25,248 --> 00:14:26,088
Ava？

305
00:14:26,288 --> 00:14:26,928
You know

306
00:14:26,968 --> 00:14:29,368
back when you were the daughter of the hospital director

307
00:14:29,408 --> 00:14:31,728
You never even
gave me the time of day

308
00:14:32,008 --> 00:14:34,649
Who would have
thought that you'd even think to call？

309
00:14:36,449 --> 00:14:38,049
I understand
you're well off

310
00:14:38,089 --> 00:14:39,209
But really

311
00:14:39,289 --> 00:14:40,289
I think you're
getting lonely

312
00:14:40,329 --> 00:14:41,209
aren't you？

313
00:14:41,249 --> 00:14:42,770
I mean it
when I say it，Eva

314
00:14:42,810 --> 00:14:44,370
I'm more than
happy to listen

315
00:14:44,410 --> 00:14:45,570
anytime

316
00:14:46,050 --> 00:14:46,410
Look

317
00:14:46,450 --> 00:14:48,530
I don't want you
to let them meet up

318
00:14:50,009 --> 00:14:53,015
Dr Tenma and the
state senator's daughter

319
00:14:53,698 --> 00:14:55,421
Don't let
him meet her

320
00:14:56,746 --> 00:14:57,267
Man

321
00:14:57,307 --> 00:14:58,510
I should
have known

322
00:14:58,550 --> 00:15:00,433
You're still
in love with him

323
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:03,841
Don't let him…

324
00:15:30,127 --> 00:15:31,126
Do me a favour

325
00:15:31,166 --> 00:15:32,646
don't screw
it up this time

326
00:15:32,686 --> 00:15:34,686
I went out of my
way to set this one up for you

327
00:15:34,726 --> 00:15:35,646
Tenma

328
00:15:36,566 --> 00:15:38,846
Well，we'll
see about that

329
00:15:45,205 --> 00:15:46,125
This is it

330
00:15:46,165 --> 00:15:49,844
This is the clock
that Mr， Yunker's was talking about at the hospital

331
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:53,540
Excuse me

332
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:54,663
about the clock
你已經遲到

333
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:55,304
喂，what's going on？

334
00:15:55,344 --> 00:15:56,185
你已經遲到

335
00:16:25,133 --> 00:16:27,213
That's a very
beautiful watch

336
00:16:27,253 --> 00:16:29,933
Oh，Why，thank you

337
00:16:30,293 --> 00:16:31,613
I mean
I wear a watch

338
00:16:31,653 --> 00:16:32,693
but mine
is nothing

339
00:16:32,733 --> 00:16:33,973
a trinket

340
00:16:34,013 --> 00:16:34,653
Honestly

341
00:16:34,693 --> 00:16:37,093
I don't even
check the time anymore

342
00:16:37,733 --> 00:16:39,213
I wonder why

343
00:16:39,493 --> 00:16:42,653
Time seems to be
moving faster and faster

344
00:16:43,254 --> 00:16:45,137
Um，excuse me，but…

345
00:16:45,177 --> 00:16:46,377
who are you？

346
00:16:46,418 --> 00:16:47,140
I'm sorry

347
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:48,502
I don't
mean to be rude

348
00:16:48,542 --> 00:16:50,505
But are you
Senator Burger's daughter

349
00:16:50,545 --> 00:16:51,586
Angelica？

350
00:16:51,626 --> 00:16:52,387
Yes？

351
00:16:52,427 --> 00:16:53,309
Goodness

352
00:16:53,349 --> 00:16:54,951
you're a
pretty little thing

353
00:16:54,991 --> 00:16:55,632
Well aren't you？

354
00:16:55,672 --> 00:16:57,515
Uh，thank you

355
00:16:57,555 --> 00:16:58,756
I think

356
00:17:00,599 --> 00:17:03,764
And you're convinced that the entire world revolves around you

357
00:17:03,804 --> 00:17:05,045
am I right？

358
00:17:07,175 --> 00:17:10,379
Going through life thinking that there's nothing you can't have

359
00:17:10,419 --> 00:17:12,300
It must be
very pleasant

360
00:17:13,462 --> 00:17:14,664
I'm sorry

361
00:17:14,704 --> 00:17:16,146
what are you
trying to say？

362
00:17:16,186 --> 00:17:17,187
I'm confused

363
00:17:17,227 --> 00:17:18,909
who are
you exactly？

364
00:17:18,949 --> 00:17:22,392
I have this tiny
little birthmark on my inner thigh

365
00:17:23,154 --> 00:17:24,955
He used to kiss it

366
00:17:27,199 --> 00:17:30,201
How he used to
love kissing me there

367
00:17:30,483 --> 00:17:32,044
Dr Tenma，that is

368
00:17:32,084 --> 00:17:33,245
You know him？

369
00:17:43,906 --> 00:17:44,946
Oh no

370
00:17:46,026 --> 00:17:46,907
See？See？

371
00:17:46,947 --> 00:17:48,387
She left
because you were late

372
00:17:48,427 --> 00:17:51,628
and it's all
because you had to stop in that store

373
00:17:51,708 --> 00:17:53,269
Oh，too bad

374
00:17:53,309 --> 00:17:54,989
I'm sorry
about that

375
00:17:55,109 --> 00:17:57,990
Can you do me a
favour and apologise for me？

376
00:17:58,990 --> 00:18:01,271
Wait，hey，Tenma

377
00:18:07,849 --> 00:18:09,853
Maybe if you give
her a call right now

378
00:18:09,893 --> 00:18:11,374
she might
come back

379
00:18:11,856 --> 00:18:13,097
Who knows？

380
00:18:13,339 --> 00:18:15,663
I want to stop by
the hospital for a quick minute

381
00:18:15,703 --> 00:18:17,545
What？At this hour？

382
00:18:19,069 --> 00:18:21,031
Ah，I've had
it with you

383
00:18:23,998 --> 00:18:25,639
Fine，leave

384
00:18:49,380 --> 00:18:53,502
Kenzo，你係我…

385
00:18:55,943 --> 00:18:57,343
你係我嘅全部

386
00:18:57,663 --> 00:19:00,464
Mr， Junger's，請等我

387
00:19:04,505 --> 00:19:06,066
Mr， Junger's

388
00:19:10,948 --> 00:19:11,988
Kenzo，發生咩事啊？

389
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:16,440
Wait，Kenzo

390
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:18,360
I have to
talk to you

391
00:19:22,561 --> 00:19:24,081
Mr， Yunker's

392
00:19:24,682 --> 00:19:25,762
Kenzo

393
00:19:26,042 --> 00:19:27,802
please just wait

394
00:19:46,718 --> 00:19:47,639
Kenzo？

395
00:20:10,292 --> 00:20:10,972
Oh，great

396
00:20:11,012 --> 00:20:12,572
I broke my heel

397
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:28,461
Kenzou

398
00:20:56,399 --> 00:20:57,239
健仔

399
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:32,681
I saw him

400
00:21:32,721 --> 00:21:33,801
you know

401
00:21:33,921 --> 00:21:35,122
Oh yes

402
00:21:35,362 --> 00:21:37,723
a year ago
in Dusseldorf

403
00:21:37,763 --> 00:21:39,364
I saw him

404
00:21:39,645 --> 00:21:40,685
It was Johann

405
00:21:40,725 --> 00:21:41,606
I'm sure of it

406
00:22:06,558 --> 00:22:08,799
你殺咗約翰，嗬？

407
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:12,440
Guess I'll…

408
00:22:13,001 --> 00:22:14,401
Have to kill you

